    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. The log confirms the mechanism working: owner `a` was created (id=11), then owner `b` with the same telephone was rejected \u2014 `Duplicate owner identity ... +61400000004||` (same normalized telephone, empty email, empty household segment \u2192 identical whole key \u2192 409).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key formula** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.buildIdentityKey`):\n`normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + householdComponent`\n\nThe household segment carries the owner's `householdId` only when the request opts into a shared household (`sharesHousehold=true`); otherwise it is empty. This is what makes the spec's two requirements consistent:\n- **Same telephone, different household, no email** \u2192 keys equal (household segment empty for both) \u2192 **409**, matching the test `coreRejectsIdentityCollision`.\n- **Same household, different telephone** \u2192 keys differ on the telephone segment \u2192 **both allowed**, matching the spec's stated behavior change.\n\nRejection is now a single check: reject with 409 only when the new owner's whole `identityKey` exactly equals an existing owner's stored key.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 replaced the three separate checks (`isDuplicateTelephone` / `isDuplicateEmail` / `isDuplicateHousehold` and `rejectDuplicateOwner`) with `buildIdentityKey` + a single whole-key `rejectDuplicateOwner(String)`. The `householdId` is now computed before the check so it's available to the key.\n- `Owner` model \u2014 added the `identityKey` field/getter/setter (`@Column identity_key`), stored on create and auto-mapped to `OwnerDto` by MapStruct.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (so it's returned).\n- Schema SQL (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `identity_key` column; fixed the positional hsqldb seed inserts to include the new column.\n- Advice \u2014 replaced the three `DuplicateOwner{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes and handlers with a single `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 409 with `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`.\n\n`mvn test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne note worth flagging: the pre-existing MySQL `data.sql` already used positional inserts with fewer values than its schema's columns (broken before this change); since MySQL isn't exercised by the test suite, I left it as-is rather than reworking unrelated seed data.",
